  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. Read http_profile.delegated_signing_custody, proxy.delegated_signing_credential and proxy.response_signing. custody/signing_window.rs and window_emission.rs, which hold SigningWindow and its private expires, are unchanged. custody/active_key/mod.rs moved the four credential attestation checks into attestation.rs (holds_the_key, names_the_identity, echoes_the_request, window_is_admissible) in the same order with the same single DelegationCredentialInvalid refusal; window_is_admissible states the three old window conditions and the activation condition as nbf < exp, nbf <= requested.nbf, exp <= requested.exp and exp > requested.nbf, the exact negations of the old refusals. IssuanceRequest groups the arguments. The custody tests share setup helpers with the same operands. The owner signature at the claim's current text, owner-signature:thm-0063-step-7-round-5, still backs the claim text. The claim, premises and dependencies are unchanged. Evidence class as registered; V0 units are tested and probed, not machine-checked proofs. The mutation lane was not re-run by this reading; check-registries resolves every probe anchor, and every tested symbol the unit names still names a test function.",
